        "\n",
        "Please escrever five factual questions about this document that can be answered with reference to isso and without any outside knowledge. para each question, give three wrong answers and the right answer. Always put the correct answer first. escrever 4 non-numerical questions and one numerical one. Make sure the wrong answers are highly detailed. Put the question inside <Question N></Question N> tags, and the answers inside <Answers N></Answers N> tags, where N is the index of the question, as in the Exemplos. \n",
        "\n",
        "Guidelines:\n",
        "Make sure that each question clearly and independently identifies the section/minutes/government meeting from which isso derives; avoid terms like \"this document\", \"this passage\", \"this notice\" in favor of more specific descriptions. The goal is to future-proof the questions and answers in the event that they became divorced from their subject in the filing system.\n",
        "Make the questions specific to their source text. Eschew generic questions about date of publication or nome of agency. Instead, prefer questions that could not apply to notes produced by any other department/agency.\n",
        "\n",
        "Assistant:\n",
        "\"\"\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "A key detail para pay attention para in the prompt acima: the instruction para make the wrong answers \"highly detailed\". sem este instruction, the wrong answers tended para be relatively short e the direita answer stood out on comprimento alone. Put a pin in the instruction para \"Certifique-se aquele each question clearly e independently identifies the section/minutes/government meeting de qual isso derives\"; we'll come atrás para isso mais tarde.\n\nagora, we'll make a dataframe com a column onde we fill in the prompt modelo para each chunk, excluding the two chunks we used in the two-shot."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 5,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [
        {
          "nome": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "86\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "chunks = [c para c in chunks se example_passage1[20:80] not in c and example_passage2[20:80] not in c]\n",
        "df = pd.DataFrame(\n",
        "    {'chunk': chunks, 'chunk_idx': range(len(chunks))}\n",
        ")\n",
        "df['prompt'] = [mc_qa3.formatar(\n",
        "    example_passage1=example_passage1, example_passage2=example_passage2, questions1=questions1, questions2=questions2, test_passage=c\n",
        "    ) para c in chunks]\n",
        "imprimir(len(df))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "In este notebook, we'll use Claude Instant, qual has a 100K context janela just like Claude 2. You can also executar isso com Claude 2 para similar results. primeiro, we design helper code para allow us para call the api in parallel se your org allows. se não, you can just definir the CapacityLimiter para 1."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 6,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "def get_completion(client, prompt, max_tokens=3000, model='claude-instant-1.2', temperature=0):\n",
        "    retornar client.completions.create(\n",
        "        prompt=prompt, max_tokens_to_sample=max_tokens, model=model, temperature=temperature, stop_sequences=['\\n\\nHuman:', '\\n\\nAssistant:']\n",
        "    ).completion\n",
        "\n",
        "assíncrono def process_case(limiter, client, prompt, results, output_col_name='completion'):\n",
        "\n",
        "    assíncrono with limiter:\n",
        "        completion = aguardar trio.to_thread.run_sync(get_completion, client, prompt)\n",
        "\n",
        "    results.anexar({'prompt': prompt, output_col_name: completion})\n",
        "\n",
        "    se len(results) % 10 == 0:\n",
        "        imprimir(f\"{len(results)} teste cases processed\")  # Optional \"progress bar\"\n",
        "\n",
        "assíncrono def get_completions_parallel(client, prompts, output_col_name='completion'):\n",
        "    assíncrono with trio.open_nursery() as nursery:\n",
        "        limiter = trio.CapacityLimiter(10)  # definir this to the maximum concurrency allowed on your api key, which may just be 1.\n",
        "        results = []\n",
        "        para prompt in prompts:\n",
        "            nursery.start_soon(process_case, limiter, CLIENT, prompt, results, output_col_name)\n",
        "    retornar results"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": nulo,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# obter questions and answers para every prompt\n",
        "qas = aguardar get_completions_parallel(CLIENT, df.prompt.values, output_col_name='qas')\n",
        "df = df.merge(pd.DataFrame(qas), on='prompt')"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "próximo, we'll do alguns minor cleanup on the saída:\n- remover the numbers para ease of reshuffling\n- Extract the material entre XML tags\n- Make a separate row para every (question + answers) pair"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 8,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "def remove_numbered_bullets(answer):\n",
        "    retornar re.sub(r'^\\d+\\. ', '', answer)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 9,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "def extract_between_tags(tag: str, texto: str, limpar: bool = verdadeiro, alt=verdadeiro) -> list[str]:\n",
        "    # Helper função para parsing Claude's output\n",
        "    tentar:\n",
        "        ext_list = re.findall(f\"<{tag}\\s?>(.+?)</{tag}\\s?>\", texto, re.DOTALL)\n",
        "        se limpar:\n",
        "            ext_list = [e.limpar() para e in ext_list]\n",
        "        se alt and not ext_list:\n",
        "            ext_list = re.findall(f\"<{tag}\\s?>(.+?)<{tag}\\s?>\", texto, re.DOTALL)\n",
        "            se limpar:\n",
        "                ext_list = [e.limpar() para e in ext_list]\n",
        "        retornar ext_list\n",
        "    except:\n",
        "        retornar extract_between_tags(tag, texto+'</' + tag + '>', limpar, alt)\n",
        "\n",
        "def extract_answer(sample):\n",
        "    retornar extract_between_tags('Answer', sample)[0][0] se extract_between_tags(\n",
        "        'Answer', sample) senão extract_between_tags('Answer', sample + '</Answer>')[0][0] se extract_between_tags('Answer', sample + '</Answer>') senão '_'\n",
        "\n",
        "def extract_qs_as(qas, n=5):\n",
        "    # Parse each of Claude's answers to the QA generation prompt into a question and a list of answers.\n",
        "    flattened_qas = []\n",
        "    para i in range(1, n + 1):\n",
        "        tentar:\n",
        "            question = extract_between_tags(f'Question {i}', qas)[0]\n",
        "            answers = extract_between_tags(f'Answers {i}', qas)[0]\n",
        "        except:\n",
        "            continuar\n",
        "        flattened_qas.anexar({\n",
        "          'question': question,\n",
        "          'right_answer': remove_numbered_bullets(answers.dividir('\\n')[0].limpar()),\n",
        "          'wrong_answers': [remove_numbered_bullets(a.limpar()) para a in answers.dividir('\\n')[1:]]\n",
        "        })\n",
        "    retornar flattened_qas"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "We started out com 86 sections depois devoting 2 of the original 88 para Exemplos, yielding 86 * 5 = 430 questions."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 10,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [
        {
          "nome": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "430\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "qs_as = df['qas'].apply(extract_qs_as)\n",
        "df['questions'] = [[q['question'] para q in qa] para qa in qs_as]\n",
        "df['right_answers'] = [[q['right_answer'] para q in qa] para qa in qs_as]\n",
        "df['wrong_answers'] = [[q['wrong_answers'] para q in qa] para qa in qs_as]\n",
        "qa_df_rows = []\n",
        "para i, row in df.iterrows():\n",
        "    para j, q in enumerate(row.questions):\n",
        "        qa_df_rows.anexar(row.to_dict() | {'question': q, 'right_answer': row['right_answers'][j], 'wrong_answers_q': row['wrong_answers'][j]})\n",
        "qa_df = pd.DataFrame(qa_df_rows)\n",
