    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### teste tempo"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "agora para the long context part! We will criar long contexts by taking random chunks until we've made a nice big pile of tokens. We will criar a different long context para each question. We tentar two different prompts aqui: one basic prompt, e one including a \"scratchpad\" onde we ask Claude para pull relevant quotes de the document aquele may be helpful."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 26,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "mc_answer_one_chunk_prompt = \"\"\"\\n\\nHuman: Please ler the following government record closely and then answer the multiple choice question below.\n",
        "<Government Record>\n",
        "{chunk}\n",
        "</Government Record>\n",
        "Here is the question:\n",
        "<Question>\n",
        "{question}\n",
        "</Question>\n",
        "Based on the government record above, selecionar the correct answer to the question from the list below and escrever the corresponding letter (A, B, C, or D) in <Answer></Answer> tags.\n",
        "<Answers>\n",
        "{answers}\n",
        "</Answers>\n",
        "\n",
        "Assistant: Based on the government record provided, the correct answer to the question is:\n",
        "\"\"\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 27,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "mc_answer_one_chunk_prompt_scratchpad = \"\"\"\\n\\nHuman: Please ler the following government record closely and then answer the multiple choice question below.\n",
        "<Government Record>\n",
        "{chunk}\n",
        "</Government Record>\n",
        "Now here is the question para you to answer:\n",
        "<Question>\n",
        "{question}\n",
        "</Question>\n",
        "Pull 2-3 relevant quotes from the record that pertain to the question and escrever them inside <scratchpad></scratchpad> tags. Then, selecionar the correct answer to the question from the list below and escrever the corresponding letter (A, B, C, or D) in <Answer></Answer> tags.\n",
        "<Answers>\n",
        "{answers}\n",
        "</Answers>\n",
        "\n",
        "Assistant:\n",
        "\"\"\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "para criar long contexts, we use a technique we call \"randomized collage\" -- iniciar com the relevant chunk, concatenate random chunks until we reach the máximo comprimento we want para teste on, randomize the chunks, então move the relevant chunk para the desired location in the collage. We will experiment com putting the relevant chunk in the beginning, meio, e beginning of the context."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": nulo,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "def create_long_context(chunk, other_chunks, main_chunk_idx, max_tokens=70000):  # Can also use 95000.\n",
        "    doc_len = len(tokenizer.codificar(chunk))\n",
        "    chunks_ctx = [chunk]\n",
        "    np.random.shuffle(other_chunks)\n",
        "    i = 0\n",
        "    # Add chunks until we exceed the context length\n",
        "    enquanto doc_len < max_tokens:\n",
        "        chunks_ctx.anexar(other_chunks[i])\n",
        "        doc_len += len(tokenizer.codificar(other_chunks[i]))\n",
        "        i += 1\n",
        "    # Put the relevant chunk in the desired position.\n",
        "    chunks_ctx = chunks_ctx[:-1]\n",
        "    chunks_ctx_ordered = chunks_ctx[1:main_chunk_idx] + [chunk] + chunks_ctx[main_chunk_idx:]\n",
        "    retornar '\\n\\n\\n\\n'.juntar(chunks_ctx_ordered)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 29,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "qa_df['long_context_end'] = qa_df.apply(lambda row: create_long_context(row['chunk'], [c para c in chunks se c != row['chunk']], len(chunks)), axis=1)\n",
        "qa_df['long_context_middle'] = qa_df.apply(lambda row: create_long_context(row['chunk'], [c para c in chunks se c != row['chunk']], 20), axis=1)\n",
        "qa_df['long_context_beginning'] = qa_df.apply(lambda row: create_long_context(row['chunk'], [c para c in chunks se c != row['chunk']], 0), axis=1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 30,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Create prompts para each question/context\n",
        "qa_df['qa_long_ctx_prompt_end'] = qa_df.apply(lambda row: mc_answer_one_chunk_prompt.formatar(\n",
        "    chunk=row['long_context_end'], question=row['question'], answers=row['randomized_answers']),\n",
        "    axis=1\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "qa_df['qa_long_ctx_prompt_middle'] = qa_df.apply(lambda row: mc_answer_one_chunk_prompt.formatar(\n",
        "    chunk=row['long_context_middle'], question=row['question'], answers=row['randomized_answers']),\n",
        "    axis=1\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "qa_df['qa_long_ctx_prompt_beginning'] = qa_df.apply(lambda row: mc_answer_one_chunk_prompt.formatar(\n",
        "    chunk=row['long_context_beginning'], question=row['question'], answers=row['randomized_answers']),\n",
        "    axis=1\n",
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "agora we'll do another round of sampling para beginning, meio, e end. \n\n*Nota: Each of estes cells takes a enquanto para executar.* se you're just following along para fun, you probably want para executar este only on a poucos rows of qa_df."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 31,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "assíncrono def sample_from_prompt(exp_name, prompt_col):\n",
        "    global qa_df\n",
        "    answers = aguardar get_completions_parallel(CLIENT, qa_df[prompt_col].values, output_col_name=exp_name)\n",
        "    qa_df = qa_df.merge(pd.DataFrame(answers), left_on=prompt_col, right_on='prompt', suffixes=['', '_x'], how='left').drop(columns=['prompt_x'])\n",
        "    qa_df[exp_name] = [extract_answer(sample) para sample in qa_df[exp_name].values]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": nulo,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# We reuse this code block throughout to first sample each prompt and obter Claude's answer to each question, then analyze the results\n",
        "# ...and to do this para the relevant chunk being in the beginning, middle, or end.\n",
        "# NOTA: para a table with results para each row, see the blog post on Anthropic's website.\n",
        "# NOTA: se this block takes unacceptably long para you, you can downsample qa_df.\n",
        "para position in ['beginning', 'middle', 'end']:\n",
        "    exp_name = 'qa_answers_long_ctx_' + position\n",
        "    prompt_col = 'qa_long_ctx_prompt_' + position\n",
        "    _ = aguardar sample_from_prompt(exp_name, prompt_col)\n",
